Hey Marek,

I dived into it and it is indeed a very interesting case but there is no overcharge. Let me try to explain:

In April 2022, client took 8717.32 Kč worth of rides (check the statement & CSV for April). However, we charged the client 8390 Kč for this month (difference is 327.32 Kč):

!Screenshot 2023-03-06 at 02.52.32.png|width=1120,height=32!

This is because 2 rides were charged right before we took the monthly amount from their card in May (probably they made some changes related to credit cards in those days so two rides in the amount of 180Kč and 165Kč were charged immediately - 165Kč ride was charged partially 147.32 Kč). Our system, immediately having these 2 rides' payments already, added it to client’s balance so we charged them 327.32 Kč less for the month of April. Please note we reduced this amount from their April payment. So, these 2 rides were still added to the May statement as expected.

In a nutshell:

{{April usage: 8717.32}}

{{April charged: -8390}}

{{May usage: 2198.05}}

{{May charge: -2198.05 - 327.32}}

{{= 0.}}

