Hey, thank you all! Please see the proposed [process|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/6336097318930] updates below. At the moment, we’ve mentioned in the process that we won’t give out any info via a phone call, so this needs to be changed globally then (not just for TH).

h3. *How to handle authority requests?*

*Step 1: Verify the request format*

*Phone call*

{color:#bf2600}*Information for* {color}🇹🇭{color:#bf2600} *TH:*{color}{color:#bf2600} You may receive phone calls from DLT (Department of Land and Transport). DLT is considered an authority in TH, so the same process applies as with police requests. Before giving out any information, ask the DLT representative to verify the passcode.{color}

* -Ask the requester to send a written request including the below requirements to the applicable- [-country/city email address-|https://bolt.eu/en/cities/] 
** -Even if it’s a life-death situation, we still cannot provide any information via the phone as it could result in a data breach. Ask the requester to send a written request.-
* {color:#bf2600}Determine if the request indicates immediate danger to life{color}
** {color:#bf2600}*If yes*{color}{color:#bf2600}, ask the requester to:{color}
*** {color:#bf2600}Send an email to the applicable {color}[{color:#bf2600}+country/city email address+{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/cities/]{color:#bf2600} including their phone number;{color}
*** {color:#bf2600}Ensure that the email address has a domain extension of an approved agency and that they’re calling from that same number that was sent to us via email;{color}
*** {color:#bf2600}Only then you can share the following details:{color}
**** {color:#bf2600}The full name of the passenger and driver;{color}
**** {color:#bf2600}Phone numbers;{color}
**** {color:#bf2600}Email addresses; and{color}
**** {color:#bf2600}If they ask for this data: the last journey details that is related to the incident.{color}
** {color:#bf2600}*If no,*{color}{color:#bf2600} ask them to send a written DPA request to applicable {color}[{color:#bf2600}+country/city email address+{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/cities/]{color:#bf2600} including their phone number.{color}

If the process updates are OK, we can see where to add the information about the passcode(s) for Thailand (either in the same article or have them under the Country Information and then add the relevant link to the process). We can think about this once it’s confirmed that this option will be used.

